  "legend": {
    "*1*": "There is no additional exam registration - the registration for the module (confirmed by the Master Office) is also the registration to the regular exam session. The exams are held in written form (120 minutes). The regular exams generally take place on the same day as the lessons have been. Exception: Exams of the context modules normally take place on Friday. Please note: The exam period may vary from the lesson period.",
    "*2*": "A separate compulsory registration is necessary to attend the resit exam session. Only modules offered on the last regular exam session are available. Resit exams are held either in written (120 minutes) or in oral form (30 minutes) - Students cannot choose! The resit exams generally take place on the same day as the lessons have been.",
    "general": "Only the holidays / lecture-free days mentioned above are valid. No additional cantonal or municipal holidays will be considered."
  }
